            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The invention pertains to a composite material, comprising a plurality of compatible glass fibers in a thermoplastic polymer matrix, wherein the glass fibers and the polymer matrix are biocompatible and resorbable. The invention further pertains to a method for obtaining a solid polymer composite material comprising a plurality of biocompatible and resorbable glass fibers ,which are embedded in a biocompatible and resorbable matrix polymer, wherein the matrix polymer is applied from solution and the solvent of said solution is at least partially removed using an anti-solvent.</p>
            </abstract>
